STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md-8-## Architecture decisions carried into the tasks
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md-9-
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md-10-1. Curator selects Go from an absolute `CURATOR_GO`, then `GOROOT/bin/go`, then `runtime.GOROOT()/bin/go`. It never searches user `PATH`, project shims, package content, or repository-local executables.
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md-11-2. Portable cache identity stays logical. Curator's physical manager-local layout is `<curator-home>/cache/build/go-v1/<64-hex-key>/...`, protected as implementation trusted computing base state.
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md:12:3. The all-file, length-framed `curator-build-source-v1` identity includes the root package marker and remains separate from the existing marker-excluding installed-content hash.
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md-13-4. Schema and root checks, static context exclusion, skill check, closure, collision, audit, registry, attestation, and moved-tag gates precede package-aware Go commands.
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md-14-5. Dry-run may use only removable operation-private toolchain probe state. It acquires no locks, never calls `go list` or `go build`, and mutates no persistent cache or installation state.
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md-15-6. Real operations serialize per project, build misses privately, then enter the manager-home critical section for recovery, revalidation, immutable cache publication, journaled target swaps, and consumer-last commit.
STORY-260720-3plyvy_decomposition-plan.md:16:7. Generated executables remain untrusted: installation verifies but never launches them. Managed Unix and Windows shims launch the marker-selected immutable artifact later and preserve arguments and exit status.
